      <Comment>Carboxylic acids, or carboxylates in their state under physiological pH, are the most common type of organic acids. They are carbon oxoacid acids carrying at least one -C(=O)OH group and having the structure RC(=O)OH, where R is any any monovalent functional group.</Comment>
